Q: Querying with where() and get() methods in Laravel ORM A: <p>Retrieve your data like this:</p>

<pre><code>public function showImage(){
$project=Projects::where('id','&gt;','0')-&gt;get();
return view('about')-&gt;with(compact('project'));
}
</code></pre>

<p>And then in your view file you can look through the collection like this: </p>

<pre><code>@foreach($project as $project)
 {{ $project-&gt;description }}
@endforeach
</code></pre>

Q: Jackson 3 and final Map deserialization A: <p>Add a setter</p>
<pre><code>public void setContent(Map&lt;String, Serializable&gt; content) {
    this.content.clear();
    this.content.putAll(content);
</code></pre>
